{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions","id":1405876,"title":"Why is reading quickly so difficult? (Solar Linguistics Questions)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-01T20:33:36-07:00","id":1405876,"title":"Why is reading quickly so difficult? (Solar Linguistics Questions)","content":"So, I've never really understood why Swift Sage's Eye is a Linguistics 5, Essence 3 charm. It lets you read things really quickly. That's it.<br /> <br /> The charm that lets you copy text really quickly is Linguistics 1, Essence 1, so I don't see what makes this one any different. <br /> <br /> The one that lets you perfectly memorize a book also has high prereqs and requires committed essence which, again, seems excessive.<br /> <br /> Is there a subsystem that grants books magic powers that I missed? Some aspect of the Linguistics rules that makes memorizing books really useful?<br /> <br /> Or is this just weird?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T21:30:47-07:00","id":1405879,"title":"","content":"If the minister for the Bursar of Barbarian Tribute leaves you alone in her office for sixty seconds you\u2019ve read all five scrolls on her desk, her entire logbook, and sat back down before she gets back. You can also read entire libraries in a single day. If you\u2019re going all National Treasure and you\u2019re looking for clues hidden in the history of a kingdom you could spend weeks of downtime reading every historical text and account you can find, or spend an hour speed flipping through every page and scroll. You can read 17 books the size of the Iliad in an hour. <br /> <br /> Most things in exalted are kind of a joke that should probably just be skipped over without any time constraints, so being able to read volumes of information in seconds is extremely powerful. <br /> <br /> Of course, it\u2019s also very campaign dependant, like Sail. In a rough and tumble monster hunter game set in the bordermarches? Nope, worthless. In a game where you\u2019re hunting down white collar criminals while manipulating the Empire from within the Thousand Scales? Priceless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T21:39:45-07:00","id":1405880,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd say that Swift Sage's Eye is a bit better than just &quot;reading quickly&quot;. It's reading 3 pages a <i>second</i>. That's pretty damn incredible. I consider myself a fairly quick reader, and I can read about a page a minute, depending on how deep into a book I am and how it's structured. 180 times that speed is, well, just mind-boggling. <br /> <br /> More generally, like a lot of the subsystems in Exalted, this kind of thing is situationally useful, and depends on the ST putting stuff in that's relevant. Taking the charm is something that I, as an ST, would take as a sign that you wanted that kind of challenge to come up, and put them in. I'd make a point of doing things like having your character interact with an author whose book you had handy, for instance, so that you could speed-read it in seconds and be able to talk intelligently with her about it, or provide a ticking clock where you had to find a demon's secret weakness, which would require reading through a hundred tomes of obscure lore or something.<br /> <br /> Of course, like a lot of things in the corebook, I do kinda feel that the mechanics of the charm uses a bit too much real-world stuff, and would probably be better described in more narrative terms - something like &quot;you can read a long page of text in less than a second, and only take a minute to read a lengthy tome hundreds of pages long&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T21:46:32-07:00","id":1405881,"title":"","content":"I'm going to deviate ever-so-slightly from the simian doctor's prescription; Linguistics Charms' usefulness may indeed be shaped by the nature of the chronicle into which the character has been inserted, but unless the ST is railroading <i>hard</i> to keep you away from written works or blank paper, you can <i>make</i> quite a bit of story happen with the Linguistics tree.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T21:49:40-07:00","id":1405882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1405880#post1405880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd say that Swift Sage's Eye is a bit better than just &quot;reading quickly&quot;. It's reading 3 pages a <i>second</i>. That's pretty damn incredible. I consider myself a fairly quick reader, and I can read about a page a minute, depending on how deep into a book I am and how it's structured. 180 times that speed is, well, just mind-boggling.</div> </div> </div> </div>A tidbit I happened to absorb from the Internet: Spencer Reid from TV's <i>Criminal Minds</i> has a canonical reading speed of twenty <i>thousand</i> words per minute. I'd hope he wasn't inclined to do so, but if he wanted, he could have read <i>Atlas Shrugged</i> <b>four times</b> during his lunch break, and still have time to stuff a tiny sandwich into his craw.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T23:36:52-07:00","id":1405888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1405881#post1405881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to deviate ever-so-slightly from the simian doctor's prescription; Linguistics Charms' usefulness may indeed be shaped by the nature of the chronicle into which the character has been inserted, but unless the ST is railroading <i>hard</i> to keep you away from written works or blank paper, you can <i>make</i> quite a bit of story happen with the Linguistics tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to give some examples?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T00:31:37-07:00","id":1405892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1405888#post1405888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Care to give some examples?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make a story happen with speed reading:<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm going into the Blessed Library of 1,000 Shelves and I'm going to read all 500 books about the Shogunate. I'll meet you for lunch to tell you where the lost battle of Emen-et-Un took place&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Tax records and genealogies are the best tracked things on the Isle. I'm going to blitz through them until i find a discrepancy to throw in Cathak Sidon's smug face at the party tonight&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;First Blooming Peach is going to distract the Guild Prince with the Ballad of Blue Tears, which gives me 8 minutes and 14 seconds to sneak into his office. I should have his ledgers, journals, contracts, and plans read by the time she hits the second chorus, then I'm out&quot;<br /> <br /> Think of a good &quot;introduce a fact&quot; Lore idea and then times it by 10 because in an hour you can read a fucking full undergraduate syllabus about the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T01:26:22-07:00","id":1405897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions#post1405876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've never really understood why Swift Sage's Eye is a Linguistics 5, Essence 3 charm. It lets you read things really quickly. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Shrug*<br /> <br /> Corebook Charmset.<br /> <br /> Teaching someone needs Lore 5. Making a magical disguise is Larceny 4. Ventriloquism is Performance 4.<br /> <br /> One could comfortably cap the Ability requirement for Charms at the Essence requirement for any Charm.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that this is WAAAAY faster than Whirling Brush Method.<br /> <br /> I'd still peg it at Linguistics 2 Essence 2.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Memorizing a book costs one mote and the commitment is released after you ingrain the knowledge. Plus you can always Whirling Brush your own copy. I don't think it needs to be higher than Linguistics 3 Essence 3, but I'm fine with it being an Essence 3 Charm with a mote commitment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-02-2020, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T03:28:14-07:00","id":1405909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions#post1405876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've never really understood why Swift Sage's Eye is a Linguistics 5, Essence 3 charm. It lets you read things really quickly. That's it.<br /> <br /> The charm that lets you copy text really quickly is Linguistics 1, Essence 1, so I don't see what makes this one any different.<br /> <br /> The one that lets you perfectly memorize a book also has high prereqs and requires committed essence which, again, seems excessive.<br /> <br /> Is there a subsystem that grants books magic powers that I missed? Some aspect of the Linguistics rules that makes memorizing books really useful?<br /> <br /> Or is this just weird?</div> </div> </div> </div>The comparison that stands out the most to me is in Whirling Brush Method's power for transcription. I want to say that a Solar who is reading for the sake of immediately writing while under that Charm is not really internalising what they see the way they would for Swift Sage's Eye. Either that or think that its reference to transcribing a large book in just a day is a bit understated and it would logically take longer.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I would see something valid in the Charm having higher Essence, because it's allowing you to draw something extant in the world to yourself in a manner that can be empowering beyond the effect of the Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T11:20:54-07:00","id":1405972,"title":"","content":"There's an episode of Burn Notice where a former spy and the protagonist's mom need to get access to a police detective's computer to find out how much evidence the cops have on a specific investigation. They get a meeting with the cop by lying that the protagonist's mom might be able to identify a suspect in an ongoing case. When they're there, the former spy and the cop go to a vending machine while the mom looks at mug shots (and accesses the cop's laptop). The former spy has to keep the cop at the vending machine as long as possible to buy time. <br /> <br /> If you can read or forge/fabricate documents in seconds, a lot of spy work becomes <i>much</i> easier and safer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T00:22:49-07:00","id":1406392,"title":"","content":"Linguistic Charms have some oddities. Personally, I would like to know how fusing multiple languages (Mingled Tongue Technique) or having the ability to be understood by all with a language that has no words, letters, or mechanics (Single Voice Kata) is considered to be easier than just learning a language at a rapid pace (Excellent Emissary's Tongue). I would have put them as Excellent Emissary's Tongue -&gt; Mingled Tongue Technique -&gt; Single Voice Kata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T12:35:35-07:00","id":1406489,"title":"","content":"That tree is especially amusing when you notice that DBs do it arguably better for half as many Charm purchases (Thousand Tongues Meditation). Of course IMO both compare pretty unfavorably to just buying the dang Language merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T16:59:51-07:00","id":1406694,"title":"","content":"Lunar Perception - Scrutiny: Untangling The Web. 3m, Perception 2, Essence 1, lets you read one page of text in one second and longer texts in one to ten minutes (so it cannot go higher than ten minutes per single book) plus adds bonuses to deciphering codes plus adds a niche read intentions bonus. You could easily just use these rules to eyeball what quick-reading effects should have as prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T23:15:38-07:00","id":1406728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406694#post1406694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Perception - Scrutiny: Untangling The Web. 3m, Perception 2, Essence 1, lets you read one page of text in one second and longer texts in one to ten minutes (so it cannot go higher than ten minutes per single book) plus adds bonuses to deciphering codes plus adds a niche read intentions bonus. You could easily just use these rules to eyeball what quick-reading effects should have as prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swift Sages Eye lets you read three times faster than that at a third of the mote cost. It's also Reflexive, rather than Supplemental, and Mute.<br /> <br /> I still strongly feel like it shouldn't be a 5/3 Charm with three prereqs. But it's way above a 2/1 Charm with no prereqs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T02:23:24-07:00","id":1406732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406728#post1406728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swift Sages Eye lets you read three times faster than that at a third of the mote cost. It's also Reflexive, rather than Supplemental, and Mute.<br /> <br /> I still strongly feel like it shouldn't be a 5/3 Charm with three prereqs. But it's way above a 2/1 Charm with no prereqs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the 3 times faster is really &quot;not useful&quot;, because I think most ST handles times in RPG's as &quot;you make it in time&quot; or &quot;you don't make it in time&quot;. I rarely see people literally saying &quot;He'll be gone for precisely 5 mns, so prepare a schedule of how you handle those 5 mns&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T03:20:27-07:00","id":1406735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406732#post1406732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the 3 times faster is really &amp;quot;not useful&amp;quot;, because I think most ST handles times in RPG's as &amp;quot;you make it in time&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;you don't make it in time&amp;quot;. I rarely see people literally saying &amp;quot;He'll be gone for precisely 5 mns, so prepare a schedule of how you handle those 5 mns&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug*<br /> <br /> Is reading faster useful at all then?<br /> <br /> And are you never going to be in a speed reading competition with a Lunar? Or some god or Dragon-Blooded when the extra speed would make a difference?<br /> <br /> And let's not forget the wealth of dedicated linguistics Charms Solars get with this -- like memorizing the book, changing its text, writing other texts in the tone of the author, transcribing a perfect copy. Lunars get some good forgery effects, but nothing like what Solars get.<br /> <br /> All I'm saying is that the existence of a similiar Lunar Charm which is more broadly applicable but less powerful doesn't change how I rate the Solar Charm. I don't think this should be Linguistics 2 Essence 1. YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T04:33:47-07:00","id":1406740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406735#post1406735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug*<br /> <br /> Is reading faster useful at all then?<br /> <br /> And are you never going to be in a speed reading competition with a Lunar? Or some god or Dragon-Blooded when the extra speed would make a difference?<br /> <br /> And let's not forget the wealth of dedicated linguistics Charms Solars get with this -- like memorizing the book, changing its text, writing other texts in the tone of the author, transcribing a perfect copy. Lunars get some good forgery effects, but nothing like what Solars get.<br /> <br /> All I'm saying is that the existence of a similiar Lunar Charm which is more broadly applicable but less powerful doesn't change how I rate the Solar Charm. I don't think this should be Linguistics 2 Essence 1. YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>We apparently misunderstood each other so I'll try to be more clear with a specific example on another subject.<br /> <br /> Take travel distance and time. It's good to have a Charm that says &quot;You can travel in one day instead of one week&quot;, but I think it's not really different than &quot;You can travel in 2 days instead of 1 week&quot;, because most ST do not account for the specific of time and distance, and are more usually working with time periods (days, weeks, months, years, decades, centuries ...). I don't think I've ever seen any situation in my gaming life where the ST was like &quot;Well thanks to your speed superpower you made it in specifically 4 days and I set my timer at 4 days and a half and no more so you succeeded, but you wouldn't if your superpower allowed you to do this in at best 5 days&quot;. <br /> <br /> I mostly agree with the rest of what you said and think it's good to have Charms like that, but I think it's also good to recognize that for a lot of people (at least that I know of) some of the specifics of these Charms are not useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T05:03:27-07:00","id":1406743,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, I agree with you.<br /> <br /> There are specific circumstances where it does matter, but I agree that it normally doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T06:51:41-07:00","id":1406756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406728#post1406728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swift Sages Eye lets you read three times faster than that at a third of the mote cost. It's also Reflexive, rather than Supplemental, and Mute.<br /> <br /> I still strongly feel like it shouldn't be a 5/3 Charm with three prereqs. But it's way above a 2/1 Charm with no prereqs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For an effect as niche as &quot;read fast&quot; without any other uses, no, it should at best be Linguistics 1 Essence 1 no prereqs. Literally no game I've been in has involved reading something as part of the plot, let alone reading something super fast due to some time limit, and I've been in a ton of them. Reflexive rather than supplemental means literally nothing for its purposes, and Mute also means nothing since it's 1m and you're not using any other Charm to enhance the speed reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T07:16:39-07:00","id":1406760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406756#post1406756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally no game I've been in has involved reading something as part of the plot, let alone reading something super fast due to some time limit, and I've been in a ton of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>In how many of those games was there a character who specifically brought a power to read faster?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T07:24:00-07:00","id":1406764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406760#post1406760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In how many of those games was there a character who specifically brought a power to read faster?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Let's bring a power to read faster so that the ST feels forced to shoehorn scenes about reading faster so I can make use of it&quot; Doesn't exactly make for a great counterargument to &quot;hey, maybe this Charm is way too niche to be anything but prerequisite-less&quot;. And a bunch of them had high-Linguistics characters, who used it for social influence - still no reading on their end, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T07:45:58-07:00","id":1406772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406740#post1406740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take travel distance and time. It's good to have a Charm that says &amp;quot;You can travel in one day instead of one week&amp;quot;, but I think it's not really different than &amp;quot;You can travel in 2 days instead of 1 week&amp;quot;, because most ST do not account for the specific of time and distance, and are more usually working with time periods (days, weeks, months, years, decades, centuries ...). I don't think I've ever seen any situation in my gaming life where the ST was like &amp;quot;Well thanks to your speed superpower you made it in specifically 4 days and I set my timer at 4 days and a half and no more so you succeeded, but you wouldn't if your superpower allowed you to do this in at best 5 days&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an issue that can be solved with extended rolls representing time sensitive travel, which I use all the time.<br /> <br /> You have three days to make the journey, the extended roll is difficulty 0, with a goal number of 15 and an interval of one day. Get 15 successes in 3 rolls or fail. Any sail charms that add speed add to this, and so do any athletics charms that affect tests of speed.<br /> <br /> Charms like Wind-Racing Essence Infusion give you a dice bonus to tests of speed, but also give you a speed multiplier in \u201cnarrative time\u201d. I\u2019m 90% sure what that means is that when time is not a factor and you aren\u2019t busting out the extended rolls, you can still use the charm to move blazingly fast, but I\u2019m fairly sure there are no charms in the game that just give you a speed bonus without mentioning how they affect tests of speed.<br /> <br /> As far as the speed reading goes, it doesn\u2019t provide a bonus to extended rolls but it\u2019s so absurdly fast that you can pretty much just handwave the thing anyway. It\u2019s like Lock Opening Touch, just instead of \u201coh there\u2019s a lock in our way? *poke* it\u2019s open, let\u2019s go\u201d it\u2019s \u201coh this is a record of this kingdoms historical legends? *flip flip flip* okay, got it, there were a bunch of pointless stories about their old city god who\u2019s dead now, but one veeery interesting one about an air spirit who once lived here and now doesn\u2019t, we need to track her down.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406756#post1406756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an effect as niche as &amp;quot;read fast&amp;quot; without any other uses, no, it should at best be Linguistics 1 Essence 1 no prereqs. Literally no game I've been in has involved reading something as part of the plot, let alone reading something super fast due to some time limit, and I've been in a ton of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve also been in a ton and I\u2019ve never seen strategic warfare used even once, and I\u2019ve probably only seen cover mechanics used maybe twice. I honestly can\u2019t remember a single time cover has been used in any of the games I\u2019ve been in, I\u2019m just not as 100% certain that I\u2019ve never seen it as strategic warfare. That doesn\u2019t mean that Battle Visionary\u2019s Foresight isn\u2019t a stupid OP charm, just that I\u2019ve never played in or ran a game where any of my players were great generals or involved that mechanic. <br /> <br /> It might be slightly over pre-req at Essence 3, but I wouldn\u2019t put it under Essence 2. You have to balance charms for the kinds of campaigns they\u2019ll be used in, not how often those situations come up over all campaigns. Otherwise Sail would be a very different charm tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:00:48-07:00","id":1406778,"title":"","content":"Using the Charm tree for the utterly broken system (that has non-niche Charms like Salty Dog) as an example of how things shouldn't be balanced around being niche... let's just say it's not very convincing. I have seen strategic warfare plenty. Cover isn't worth the hassle and barely any Charms interact with it, besides ignoring it as a side effect, making it even less worth the hassle. Niche Charms should definitely have less prerequisites and more focused power than broad Charms, and in this case there's an existing example in Lunars that backs this notion. Tell a player who wants to play a speed-reader that the Solar version is E2, and they'll just play a Lunar instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:26:04-07:00","id":1406784,"title":"","content":"Or play a linguistics Supernal solar and be better than the Lunar in that regard right off chargen, even if the charm is Essence 3.<br /> <br /> Cover is definitely worth the hassle, I just consistently forget about it. You get +2 non-charm bonus to defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:32:16-07:00","id":1406785,"title":"","content":"That even Dragon-Blooded excellencies ignore, let alone basic workhorses. Also, sure, waste a Supernal on speed-reading when the Lunar just picks a single Charm and gets it over with. While also getting side benefits from it. Point being, Solars and Lunars are Celestial Exalts, both should be fairly close in terms of power, and neither is exactly known for their ability to speed read (the way Solars are known for artifice and sorcery, or Lunars are known for regeneration and subterfuge, among others), so neither should have such a massive difference in their prerequisites for speed reading. Linguistics 1 or 2, Essence 1 is perfectly fine for that kind of super niche effect. I'd probably give it for free as a rider to some other Charm, in all honesty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T09:35:09-07:00","id":1406794,"title":"","content":"Solar vs. Lunar speedreading depends how you look at it. Linguistics is typically the writing Ability, not the reading Ability, so it makes a certain amount of sense that it might lend itself to reading Charms less easily than Perception does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:06:00-07:00","id":1406802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406785#post1406785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That even Dragon-Blooded excellencies ignore, let alone basic workhorses.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) most enemies you face are not even exalted, those that are aren\u2019t guaranteed to have cover ignoring charms<br /> <br /> 2) I\u2019m pretty sure Lunars don\u2019t even have a charm to ignore cover in their whole printed charmset<br /> <br /> 3) Even the Solar ones aren\u2019t just \u201cspend a mote you we\u2019re going to anyway and ignore all cover\u201d. Wise Arrow ignores one point of cover...or gives an enemy with no cover -1 defense. Which is just a roundabout way of saying -1 defense always regardless of cover or not, being in heavy cover still gives you +2 non-charm defense. The Thrown one is a damn Simple charm that costs 3m and does nothing but ignore cover. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406785#post1406785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, sure, waste a Supernal on speed-reading when the Lunar just picks a single Charm and gets it over with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal lets you do way more than just pick one charm, my Supernal linguist blows that Lunar out of the water in written social influence, language learning and writing speed, in addition to better and more efficient speed reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T11:14:49-07:00","id":1406814,"title":"","content":"Might wanna check that second point again. Originally, Lunars had Finding the Needle's Eye that let them ignore a point of Defense from cover, weapons, or Full Defense if I'm not mistaken (besides rerolling Essence 1s); currently, the Charm flat out lets them ignore a point of Defense plus the rerolls, unconditionally. Lets them attack through Full Cover with a stunt, at +3 Defense. And animal shapes with flexible appendages like tails get to ignore a second point of Defense. Three motes. And that's just one Charm I remember off the dome, I'm more than certain they've got more elsewhere. Solars are not good examples of proper balance.<br /> <br /> Point is made, speed reading is extremely niche and situational, therefore it should have minimal if any prerequisites on its own, or be a rider for a different Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T11:17:09-07:00","id":1406815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406794#post1406794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar vs. Lunar speedreading depends how you look at it. Linguistics is typically the writing Ability, not the reading Ability, so it makes a certain amount of sense that it might lend itself to reading Charms less easily than Perception does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then wouldn't it be better to just make speedreading an Awareness 1 E1 Charm and call it a day? Putting the Charm where it lends itself to best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T11:47:08-07:00","id":1406818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406815#post1406815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then wouldn't it be better to just make speedreading an Awareness 1 E1 Charm and call it a day? Putting the Charm where it lends itself to best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that you feel strongly about this. Golden Rule it to whatever you like at your table.<br /> <br /> We're not in a game together, you don't have to convince us.<br /> <br /> I think everyone here agrees Linguistics 5, Essence 3 and 3 prepress is too high. We'd don't need to agree a consensus on what it should be.<br /> <br /> For my part, I see Solar Charms like this:<br /> <br /> Essence 1 -- normal but better. &quot;Excellent Strike&quot; style Charms. Things that give an edge over mortals.<br /> Essence 3 -- the power of the Sun. Bend reality to your will with Wyld Shaping and Celestial Sorcery. Fight with the Invincible Fury of the Dawn. Seduce monks and husbands with your demon dance. Things that let you dominate gods.<br /> Essence 5 -- peak Exalted power. The Aegis of Invincible might that leaves you invulnerable to harm. Proclaim doom upon a city with Dogstar Ruminations. Slay all foes before you in a Circle of Bright Reaving. Rapters in an F16.<br /> <br /> Reading fast? Essence 1. Reading <i>as fast as you can turn the page</i>? For me, that kind of Flash speed, super reading isn't on a par with &quot;rebuild[ing] a ruined body and stand it upright in the time it takes to lace on boots&quot; (Essence 3) but seems about the same as slashing a shockwave through the air to hit a distant foe (Essence 2).<br /> <br /> It's not about how useful the Charm is, it's about how overtly magical it is (with some concessions for genre).<br /> <br /> Johnny-5ing a library is not (in my opinion) an Essence 1 effect. But it's not like Exalted is perfectly balanced game. If you want it at Essence 1, then go for it. Houserule it however you like.<br /> <br /> (And if we're talking pure canon: the Corebook Charms represent iconic Solar abilities at the peak of Solar power. That doesn't mean an Essence 1 speed reading charm can't exist: just that it can't be as powerful as three pages a second for a single mote.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-07-2020, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T12:29:28-07:00","id":1406824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406814#post1406814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might wanna check that second point again. Originally, Lunars had Finding the Needle's Eye that let them ignore a point of Defense from cover, weapons, or Full Defense if I'm not mistaken (besides rerolling Essence 1s); currently, the Charm flat out lets them ignore a point of Defense plus the rerolls, unconditionally. Lets them attack through Full Cover with a stunt, at +3 Defense. And animal shapes with flexible appendages like tails get to ignore a second point of Defense. Three motes. And that's just one Charm I remember off the dome, I'm more than certain they've got more elsewhere. Solars are not good examples of proper balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn\u2019t, in any way, negate the defense bonus for being in light or heavy cover. You\u2019ve got 5 defense out of cover, finding the needle makes it 4. You\u2019ve got 7 defense in heavy cover, finding the needle makes it 6.<br /> <br /> But okay, neither Lunars nor Solars are good places to look for balance, so let\u2019s search the DB charmtrees. Archery has Heartbeats Before Death, a willpower costing aura charm that ignores all cover bonuses as an incidental effect to reflexively aiming, and Thrown has the excellency, at last, a charm where ignoring light cover exclusively is an incidental effect to a charm you\u2019d use all the time anyway. <br /> <br /> Outside of that I don\u2019t think any demon, elemental, god, ghost, monster, animal, mortal or carnivorous plant ignores cover as a side effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T16:32:08-07:00","id":1406857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405876-why-is-reading-quickly-so-difficult-solar-linguistics-questions?p=1406815#post1406815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then wouldn't it be better to just make speedreading an Awareness 1 E1 Charm and call it a day? Putting the Charm where it lends itself to best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awareness is even less the reading Ability unless the question is how far away can you make out the words from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}